---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout title="CleanControlling — Max Vogt">
  <main id="top" class="page-container">
    <header class="section-pad fade-up">
      <div class="flex items-center justify-between gap-6">
        <label class="toggle text-base">
          <a class="text-[1.25rem] font-semibold text-[var(--color-text)] hover:text-[var(--color-primary)]" href="/">Max.</a>
          <input type="checkbox" aria-label="Toggle dark mode" data-theme-toggle />
          <span class="toggle-icons" aria-hidden="true">
            <span class="toggle-icon icon-moon">◑</span>
          </span>
        </label>
        <nav class="flex items-center gap-8 text-base">
          <a class="nav-link transition-colors duration-200 hover:text-[var(--color-primary)]" href="/">Work</a>
          <a class="nav-link transition-colors duration-200 hover:text-[var(--color-primary)]" href="/about">About</a>
          <a
            class="nav-link transition-colors duration-200 hover:text-[var(--color-primary)]"
            href="https://www.instagram.com/maaxvogt/"
            target="_blank"
            rel="noreferrer"
          >
            Fun
          </a>
        </nav>
      </div>
    </header>

    <section class="section-pad fade-up delay-1">
      <div class="flex flex-col gap-6">
        <h1 class="text-[clamp(2.8rem,6vw,4.6rem)]">CleanControlling – AI-Based PDF Comparison Pipeline</h1>
        <p class="text-lg text-muted max-w-[52rem]">
          An automated document monitoring and change-detection system that continuously compares
          regulatory PDF documents, identifies meaningful updates using deterministic diffing and
          AI-assisted semantic analysis, and proactively notifies stakeholders. The project prioritizes
          reliability, auditability, and real-world compliance workflows over heuristic or black-box
          analysis.
        </p>
        <div class="grid gap-6 md:grid-cols-3 text-sm">
          <div>
            <p class="text-muted uppercase tracking-[0.2em]">Role</p>
            <p>Software Engineer (End-to-End Ownership)</p>
          </div>
          <div>
            <p class="text-muted uppercase tracking-[0.2em]">Team</p>
            <p>Solo project in direct collaboration with business stakeholders</p>
          </div>
          <div>
            <p class="text-muted uppercase tracking-[0.2em]">Duration</p>
            <p>~3 months (design, implementation, production rollout)</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section-pad fade-up delay-2">
      <div class="case-row">
        <h2 class="case-title">Impact & Metrics</h2>
        <div class="case-body">
          <p class="text-muted">
            The system replaced a manual, error-prone review process with a fully automated, continuous
            monitoring pipeline, delivering measurable operational and compliance impact:
          </p>
          <ul class="list-disc pl-5 text-muted space-y-2">
            <li>~100% coverage of monitored vendor documents</li>
            <li>Daily automated checks, eliminating irregular manual reviews</li>
            <li>Minutes instead of hours to detect and communicate relevant changes</li>
            <li>Reduced compliance risk by ensuring stakeholders always work with the latest approved documentation</li>
            <li>Zero ongoing maintenance overhead after rollout due to containerized deployment</li>
          </ul>
          <p class="text-muted">
            The solution scaled linearly with the number of documents without increasing human workload.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section-pad">
      <div class="case-row">
        <h2 class="case-title">Brief</h2>
        <div class="case-body">
          <p class="text-muted">
            Regulatory and safety documentation changes frequently, yet many organizations still rely on
            manual checks or infrequent reviews, introducing compliance risks and unnecessary operational
            overhead.
          </p>
          <p class="text-muted">
            In this project, I designed and implemented a fully automated pipeline that continuously
            monitors vendor-provided safety data sheets, detects document changes at both structural and
            semantic levels, and distributes actionable updates to relevant stakeholders. The system
            replaces reactive, manual processes with a proactive, auditable, and scalable solution
            tailored for real compliance workflows.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section-pad">
      <div class="case-row">
        <h2 class="case-title">Technical Approach</h2>
        <div class="case-body">
          <p class="text-muted">
            The architecture was intentionally designed to prioritize determinism, traceability, and
            auditability before introducing AI-driven interpretation.
          </p>
          <p class="text-muted font-semibold">Document retrieval & versioning</p>
          <p class="text-muted">
            Vendor PDFs are periodically fetched and compared against locally versioned documents.
          </p>
          <p class="text-muted font-semibold">PDF-level diffing</p>
          <p class="text-muted">
            Structural and textual differences are analyzed to distinguish meaningful content changes
            from cosmetic updates (e.g., formatting or metadata changes).
          </p>
          <p class="text-muted font-semibold">AI-assisted semantic analysis</p>
          <p class="text-muted">
            When changes are detected, a large language model (Gemini) generates concise, human-readable
            summaries highlighting what changed and why it matters, optimized for non-technical stakeholders.
          </p>
          <p class="text-muted font-semibold">Automation & delivery</p>
          <p class="text-muted">
            The pipeline runs in a containerized environment (Docker / Docker Compose) and automatically
            distributes updated documents and summaries via email.
          </p>
          <p class="text-muted">
            This hybrid approach avoids black-box decisions while still benefiting from AI where it
            meaningfully reduces cognitive load.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section-pad">
      <div class="case-row">
        <h2 class="case-title">Learning and Growth</h2>
        <div class="case-body">
          <p class="text-muted">
            This project significantly deepened my experience in production-grade automation and applied AI:
          </p>
          <ul class="list-disc pl-5 text-muted space-y-2">
            <li>Designing systems where correctness and explainability are more important than raw model output</li>
            <li>Integrating LLMs into deterministic pipelines without sacrificing trust or auditability</li>
            <li>Building maintainable, containerized services aligned with real operational constraints</li>
            <li>Translating regulatory and compliance requirements into concrete technical guarantees</li>
          </ul>
          <p class="text-muted">
            It reinforced the importance of engineering judgment when deciding where AI should — and
            should not — be used.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section-pad">
      <div class="case-row">
        <h2 class="case-title">Takeaway</h2>
        <div class="case-body">
          <p class="text-muted font-semibold">
            Reliable software systems are not defined by how intelligent they appear, but by how predictable,
            explainable, and useful they are in real workflows.
          </p>
          <p class="text-muted">
            This project demonstrates how AI is most effective when used as a supporting layer on top of
            well-structured, deterministic systems — enhancing human decision-making rather than replacing it.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="mt-16 text-right">
        <a href="#top" class="nav-link text-base">Back to Top ↑</a>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section-pad">
      <div class="flex flex-col gap-6">
        <h2>Let's get in touch</h2>
        <p class="text-muted">
          HMU for work, coffee, or if you just want to talk.
        </p>
        <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-6 text-sm">
          <a
            class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 border-b border-transparent transition-colors duration-200 hover:border-[var(--color-primary)]"
            href="https://github.com/maaxvogt/"
            target="_blank"
            rel="noreferrer"
          >
            GitHub
          </a>
          <a
            class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 border-b border-transparent transition-colors duration-200 hover:border-[var(--color-primary)]"
            href="mailto:mavoxgt@gmail.com"
          >
            Mail
          </a>
        </div>
        <p class="text-sm text-muted">Designed and coded by Max Vogt</p>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>
</Layout>
